# Storefront conventions (`@platform/storefront`)

Folder: `client/`. npm name: `@platform/storefront`.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, Bootstrap 5 + SCSS, Zustand (cart/wishlist/compare).

## Site integration

- Resolve site via `getStorefrontSiteConfig()` / `lib/site.ts`.
- Root `/` uses `HomeLayoutRenderer` + `SiteConfig.homeLayout`.
- Theme CSS variables from `site.theme` via `SiteThemeStyles`.

## Demo vs production

- ~300 demo routes under `app/(homes)`, `(shop)`, `(product-single)`, etc.
- Static catalog: `data/products/*.ts`. API used selectively (e.g. Beauty home `Products1.tsx` with static fallback).
- Do not wire API into every demo page unless product requires it.

## Tab-driven product sections

Follow `client/.cursor/rules/product-tab-filtering-pattern.mdc`:

- `TABS` array + `activeTab` state
- Filter with `useMemo` and `product.demoTab?.includes(activeTab)`
- Never put synthetic tab ids like `view-all` into `demoTab` data

## Modals & state

- Register modals in `components/common/other-components/LayoutModals.tsx`
- Open/close via `context/uiStore.ts`
- Cart persistence: `context/store.ts`

## Quality

```bash
npm run lint -w @platform/storefront
npm run build -w @platform/storefront
```

See `docs/CONVENTIONS.md` for full patterns.
